preConditionHook:
// A BREAKOUT WITH A BUFFER. The close clears the PRIOR bar's high by at least
// offsetTicks before the entry counts -- Brooks's guard against the one-tick
// trap, "a couple of ticks above the high of the prior bar" (T04-14). Mirrored
// below the prior low.
//
// EL: close > high[1] + offsetTicks * tickSize
//
// THE OFFSET IS THE RULE. CloseAbovePriorHigh is this test at offsetTicks = 0;
// it carries only a bar lookback and no price offset, so the buffer is not
// reachable from it at any setting. The offset is instrument-specific (Brooks
// gives a couple of ticks for stocks, one tick generally), which is how
// CloseNearPriorLow's threshold is already handled in the corpus.
//
// Not CloseNearPriorLow, which reads the close against the OPPOSITE extreme of
// the prior bar and in the opposite sense. Not NoGapThroughSignalBarStop, which
// caps the *opening price* below the same level and reads the bar's *high*,
// not its close. Not
// BreakoutClearsPriorExtremeByMargin, which measures the same margin from a
// whole Highest window and from the bar's *high* rather than its close.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local. Every scratch value is a localVariables
// entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement. Deepest bar touched: 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
